
APPROACH
For this assignment, I will work with flight arrival data for Alaska Airlines and AM West across five cities: Los Angeles, Phoenix, San Diego, San Francisco, and Seattle. The dataset contains the number of flights that were either on time or delayed for each airline and city.

DATA SOURCE
The data was recreated from the flight-delay dataset provided for the assignment. I organized the data in PostgreSQL and exported the table as a CSV file named airline_performance.csv. The original data is structured in a wide format, with each city represented as a separate column.

PLANNED APPROACH
Explore the data — inspect the dataset structure and check for missing values.

Tidy the data — transform the original wide format into long format using pivot_longer().

Calculate flight counts — use dplyr to calculate total and delayed flights for each airline.

Calculate percentages — compare delay percentages overall and across the five cities.

Visualize the data — use tables and ggplot2 charts to present the comparisons.

Investigate the differences — examine why the overall comparison may differ from the city-by-city comparison, including how flight volumes are distributed across cities.

The results and findings will be presented later in the analysis and conclusion sections
